95 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The measured parameters are continuously processed by the microcontroller and compared with predefined safety limits. When an abnormal condition is detected, the system activates a relay to disconnect the load, thereby helping to prevent further damage. An LCD display, LEDs, and a buzzer provide real-time information about the operating condition and indicate the occurrence of a fault. A manual reset mechanism is also incorporated to allow the system to resume operation after the fault condition has been addressed.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
96 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 73 0 R
/E (The main objective of this project is to develop a simple, cost-effective, and microcontroller-based transformer protection and monitoring system. The project demonstrates how sensors, embedded systems, and relay-based switching can be integrated to improve transformer safety and operational reliability. The developed prototype provides a basic demonstration of automatic protection principles and can serve as a foundation for understanding more advanced transformer protection systems used in industrial power networks.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
